1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
Animation Editor Modification

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,000
The animation editor in Marvelous Designer 11 is located at the bottom of the screen.

3
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Click the triangle to see the animation editor interface.

4
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:30,000
In the previous version of Marvelous Designer, some of the details on the top of the animation editor are now moved to the right.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:38,000
But you can still find a few tools that are commonly used at the top, such as recording, playback and simulation quality.

6
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:44,000
The most prominent advantage of the animation editor is the FPS setting.

7
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:50,000
In the previous version, FPS must be set every time you import a file.

8
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,000
But now use Marvelous Designer 11.

9
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,000
You can set the FPS in the animation settings.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:00,000
Open the animation settings.

11
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,000
On the top, there will be a frame rate setting.

12
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:09,000
In Marvelous Designer 11, only the set playback area can be recorded and played.

13
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
You can set the playback area by dragging the mouse to the two ends of the yellow bar at the top of the animation layer and dragging the mouse to set the playback area.

14
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Or you can directly enter the starting and ending frames in the quick menu.

15
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:26,000
There are three options for simulation quality.

16
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Normal, animation and self-defining.

17
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:33,000
You can usually use the normal option to test the animation.

18
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,000
Use the animation option for final recording.

19
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:45,000
If you want to use a more complex simulation quality, you can enter a number greater than 6 in the preset attribute bar on the right.

20
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
You can control the width of the animation bar by controlling the bottom slider.

21
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Click and drag the left slider to the left.

22
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
You can widen the area on the left.

23
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Click and drag the right slider to the right.

24
00:01:57,000 --> 00:01:59,000
You can widen the area on the right.

25
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
When you click and drag the middle part of the slider, you can adjust the entire animation to any side.

26
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:10,000
You can also enter the number in the input box on the left and right sides of the slider to set the viewing area of the animation axis.

27
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:14,000
In Marvelous Designer 11, you can use the number of pixels.

28
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
This is a function that was not available in the previous version.

29
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:25,000
You can use the number in the input box on top of the image.

30
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
You can choose which image to use.

31
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:30,000
You can also choose to use the number on top of the image.

32
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Here you can see the number on top of it.

33
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:39,000
When you click and drag, you can adjust the image to see the image.

34
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:45,000
If you click and drag the right slider, you can set the voice.

35
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
You can assign a departure position to the lights and lights in the image.

36
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:51,000
In the right panel, you can choose to set the character position.

